        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Key terms</h2>

        {[
          { term: "High-volume UGC", def: "A production cadence of 50-300+ creator videos per month for a single brand. Describes the pace and scale of production, not the content type or delivery model." },
          { term: "Power law", def: "The distribution pattern where a tiny percentage of posts generate the vast majority of views. In short-form video, ~1.2% of posts cross 10K views, and the top 1% drives ~88% of all views." },
          { term: "Hit rate", def: "The percentage of videos that cross a defined performance threshold (e.g., 10K views, 100K views). Higher hit rate = more efficient production. Volume increases total hits even at the same hit rate." },
          { term: "Brief template", def: "A standardized content brief format for a specific video type (testimonial, tutorial, problem-solution). Enables creators to self-serve and reduces the briefing bottleneck at scale." },
          { term: "Batch shooting", def: "Filming multiple videos in a single session. A creator shooting 8-12 videos in one batch day is far more efficient than producing one video at a time." },
          { term: "Creator network", def: "A managed pool of vetted creators available for assignment. OKAD's network includes 700+ creators across niches, languages, and content styles." },
          { term: "Quality bar", def: "The minimum standard every video must meet before publishing: clear audio, adequate lighting, on-brand messaging, platform-native format, and a strong hook." },
          { term: "Volume benchmark", def: "The recommended monthly video output for a given brand stage. Startups: 20-50, growth: 50-150, scale: 150-300+." },
          { term: "Creative testing", def: "Systematically testing different hooks, formats, angles, and creators to identify what drives performance. High volume provides the raw material for testing at scale." },
          { term: "Canvas UGC", def: "A delivery model where creators post on brand-owned social accounts and get paid per view. The lowest cost-per-video model for high-volume production. See the full Canvas UGC guide." },
        ].map((item) => (
